userStories.description:
**Goal** — Build the shared metadata/listing storage facade on US-001's lock layer and expose its neutral contract from the nax-agent package entry.

**Motivation** — The terminal UI and koda must share one session store.

**Approach** — Relevant design text, verbatim:

**Move (US-001 lock layer, US-002 metadata, listing and exports).** Create `packages/nax-agent/src/session-store/` with
`session-meta.ts` (the metadata schema, `SESSION_META_MODES`,
`SESSION_ID_PATTERN`, `defaultSessionsDir`), `session-lock-guard.ts`,
`session-lock.ts` and `storage.ts`, carrying today's logic unchanged except for
the error and type contract below, plus `index.ts` re-exporting the public
names. `packages/nax-agent/src/index.ts` re-exports them. The metadata schema
uses `BashApprovalModeSchema` (`src/config/bash-approval.ts`, same three values)
for `bashApproval`. Error text uses `errorMessage` (`src/infra/errors.ts`) where
the ACP code used `messageOf`.

**Error contract.** Every refusal of `acquireLock` (a fresh lock held by another
live pid, a takeover that loses a race, and guard contention) is a `NaxError`
with code `SESSION_LOCKED`, the same message text as today
(`session in use by pid <pid>` or `session in use by another process`), and
context `{ stage: "session-store" }` plus `pid` when known.
`SessionLockGuardBusy` becomes a `NaxError` subclass with code `SESSION_LOCKED`
and message `session in use by another process`, still distinguishable with
`instanceof` by the release retry loop. An invalid list cursor is a `NaxError`
with code `SESSION_LIST_CURSOR_INVALID`, message `invalid cursor`.
`SESSION_META_UNREADABLE` keeps its code and message; its context `stage`
becomes `"session-store"`.

**Ported tests (US-001, US-002).** The moved tests replace the ACP-only
`#test/helpers/recording-logger` (`lines`) with nax-agent's `makeLogger()` from
`test/helpers/agent-logger.ts` (`calls`). The moved fixture
`test/fixtures/session-store/lock-contender.ts` imports
`#src/session-store/session-lock` and `#src/session-store/session-lock-guard`
and passes an inline no-op `AgentLogger` (it runs as a child `bun` process, not
under `bun test`); the hardening test spawns it as
`join(import.meta.dir, "../../fixtures/session-store/lock-contender.ts")`.

**Unchanged details.** `SessionListEntry.updatedAt` carries
`updatedAt ?? createdAt`, as the ACP `infoOf` does today. The moved warn and
info log lines keep the stage `"session"`; only `NaxError` contexts use
`"session-store"`.

Implementation allocation: US-001 already supplied session-lock.ts, session-lock-guard.ts and the fixture; reuse them without importing storage.ts from the lock layer. Rename StorageDeps to SessionStorageDeps and re-export its existing definition. Port storage.test.ts to test the new module and package entry, use makeLogger() directly and inspect .calls, and assert NaxError rather than RequestError. Keep existing read/write/has/remove/list behavior, file names, schema, optional costUsd, effective timestamp, offset pagination and atomic write format. Preserve decodeCursor's absent/null/empty cursor -> offset zero behavior; for a nonempty cursor use the existing Buffer decoding, digits check and safe-integer check, changing only the error contract rather than requiring canonical base64. Export neutral SessionListEntry/SessionListPage instead of importing ACP SDK. Add explicit named barrel/root exports for createSessionStorage, defaultSessionsDir, processAlive, LIST_PAGE_SIZE, LOCK_HEARTBEAT_MS, LOCK_STALE_MS, SESSION_ID_PATTERN, SESSION_META_MODES, SessionMeta, SessionMetaMode, SessionListEntry, SessionListPage, SessionStorage and SessionStorageDeps. Run bun run api:update to regenerate api/nax-agent.api.txt; do not hand-edit the snapshot. Regression tests must fail before implementation; strict three-session TDD applies.

**Scope** — In: session-meta.ts, storage.ts, session-store/index.ts, root named exports, storage.test.ts port and API snapshot. Out: lock-protocol implementation already owned by US-001; implementing readLockHolder or publicly exporting holder types (US-003); ACP consumer conversion, wire-error mapping and deletion (US-004). No new package subpath export and no change to `check:package-boundaries`; the shared storage is exported from the `@nathapp/nax-agent` package entry only. The on-disk formats do not change: `<id>.session.json` stays `schemaVersion: 1` with the same fields, `<id>.lock` keeps its body shape (nonce plus heartbeat, and legacy pid-only locks), and file names and the temp-then-rename write stay as they are. The transcript store (`createFileTranscriptStore`, `TranscriptStore`) is unchanged and not moved. Sessions-dir resolution beyond `defaultSessionsDir(configDir)` stays in the ACP server: `--sessions-dir`, `NAX_AGENT_SESSIONS_DIR` and `agentServer.sessionsDir` are read only by `nax-agent-acp/src/server/options.ts`; how the TUI resolves the directory is decided in feature F3. No mode values are added to `SESSION_META_MODES`; mapping the TUI's `guarded` and `full` modes onto it is feature F3's work.

**Interface** — Verbatim metadata target:

```typescript
export const SESSION_META_MODES = ["none", "read", "ask", "full"] as const;
export type SessionMetaMode = (typeof SESSION_META_MODES)[number];
export const SESSION_ID_PATTERN = /^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,128}$/;
export function defaultSessionsDir(configDir: string): string; // join(configDir, ".agent-server", "sessions")
export type SessionMeta = Readonly<{
  schemaVersion: 1; sessionId: string; cwd: string; mode: SessionMetaMode; model: string;
  bashApproval: BashApprovalMode; title: string | null; createdAt: string; updatedAt: string | null; costUsd?: number;
}>;
```

Verbatim final storage target (the lines explicitly labeled US-003 and the public holder types are deferred to US-003; this story implements all remaining declarations):

```typescript
export interface SessionListEntry {
  readonly sessionId: string;
  readonly cwd: string;
  readonly title: string | null;
  readonly updatedAt: string;
}
export interface SessionListPage {
  sessions: SessionListEntry[];
  nextCursor?: string;
}
export type SessionLockHolderState = "live" | "stale" | "own";
export interface SessionLockHolder {
  readonly pid: number;
  readonly startedAt: string;
  readonly heartbeatAt: string | null;
  readonly state: SessionLockHolderState;
}
export interface SessionStorage {
  readonly dir: string;
  readMeta(sessionId: string): Promise<SessionMeta | null>;
  writeMeta(meta: SessionMeta): Promise<void>;
  hasMeta(sessionId: string): Promise<boolean>;
  removeMeta(sessionId: string): Promise<void>;
  acquireLock(sessionId: string): Promise<() => Promise<void>>;
  readLockHolder(sessionId: string): Promise<SessionLockHolder | null>; // US-003
  list(query: { readonly cwd?: string | null; readonly cursor?: string | null }): Promise<SessionListPage>;
}
export interface SessionStorageDeps {
  readonly dir: string;
  readonly pid: number;
  readonly now: () => Date;
  readonly logger: AgentLogger;
  readonly setInterval?: (callback: () => void, ms: number) => ReturnType<typeof setInterval>;
  readonly isAlive?: (pid: number) => boolean;
}
export function createSessionStorage(deps: SessionStorageDeps): SessionStorage;
export function processAlive(pid: number): boolean;
export const LIST_PAGE_SIZE = 50;
```

`StorageDeps` is renamed `SessionStorageDeps`, because it becomes a public name.

Note: `SessionLockHolderState` is declared in `session-lock.ts` by US-001; `storage.ts` imports and re-exports it and never redeclares it. `readLockHolder` and `SessionLockHolder` are added by US-003, not this story.

**Goal** — Replace ACP's local storage implementation with nax-agent's shared store and preserve its existing protocol-facing behavior.

**Motivation** — The design (§6) rules out widening the allowed import list; moving the code into `@nathapp/nax-agent`, which both packages already import, is the fix.

**Approach** — Verbatim design:

**Consume and delete (US-004).** The ACP server imports `createSessionStorage`,
`SESSION_ID_PATTERN`, `defaultSessionsDir` and the types from
`@nathapp/nax-agent`; `nax-config.ts` derives `MODES` from
`SESSION_META_MODES`; `options.ts` uses `defaultSessionsDir(configDir)` for the
fallback; `registry.list` maps the neutral page to `ListSessionsResponse`;
`toRequestError` maps `SESSION_LOCKED` to `RequestError.invalidRequest` and
`SESSION_LIST_CURSOR_INVALID` to `invalidParams`, neither logged as a failure.
Then the ACP copies (`storage.ts`, `session-lock.ts`, `session-lock-guard.ts`),
their tests and the `lock-contender.ts` fixture are deleted.

**Unchanged details.** `SessionListEntry.updatedAt` carries
`updatedAt ?? createdAt`, as the ACP `infoOf` does today. The moved warn and
info log lines keep the stage `"session"`; only `NaxError` contexts use
`"session-store"`.

Implementation allocation: switch imports/types in src/server/main.ts, connection.ts, registry.ts, registry-lifecycle.ts, registry-open.ts, options.ts and nax-config.ts. Import the shared storage names only from the @nathapp/nax-agent public entry; retain unrelated existing imports such as main.ts's @nathapp/nax-agent/mcp unchanged. In nax-config.ts set MODES to SESSION_META_MODES itself, preserving object identity, ServerMode values and existing BASH_APPROVALS behavior. options.ts changes only the sessionsDir fallback, preserving flag > env > config precedence. Registry list explicitly adapts neutral sessions and optional nextCursor into the ACP response; buildAgentApp's existing guard remains the single wire-error boundary. A storage lock or cursor refusal propagated by a direct registry call now rejects with the neutral NaxError; guard/toRequestError performs the protocol conversion. Other registry refusals retain their existing error types. Unreadable metadata retains the existing generic internal-error handling.

Update test/helpers/registry-setup.ts and the imports in test/unit/server/connection-sessions.test.ts, registry-credentials.test.ts, connection.test.ts, connection-close-switch.test.ts, registry-switch.test.ts and connection-persistence.test.ts with assertions unchanged. In registry.test.ts change only the 'a session held by another live process is refused with the pid' assertion: registry.load is called directly, not through guard(), and now rejects with NaxError code SESSION_LOCKED whose message contains 'session in use by pid 4242'; leave failure() and every other assertion unchanged. Add toRequestError mapping cases in errors.test.ts, the defaultSessionsDir case in options.test.ts and MODES identity in nax-config.test.ts without modifying existing assertions. Extend the SDK connection tests to exercise buildAgentApp over registry setup using the public createSessionStorage, including a session written directly to storage with no ACP create request. Locked load/resume fixtures must have metadata but no open registry entry: write the metadata directly, or close the created session before installing the foreign legacy lock. registry-open.ts:78-89 returns an already-open entry without acquiring another lock, and that existing behavior is not changed here. Follow strict three-session TDD and demonstrate new regression assertions fail against the old behavior.

Delete src/server/storage.ts, src/server/session-lock.ts, src/server/session-lock-guard.ts, test/unit/server/storage.test.ts, test/unit/server/storage-hardening.test.ts and test/fixtures/lock-contender.ts after switching consumers; their tests have been ported by US-001/US-002. The removals are checked by bun run typecheck and bun run check:all in packages/nax-agent-acp and review, not acceptance criteria. No new files are required.

**Scope** — In: ACP import rewiring, neutral-page protocol adaptation, two expected-error mappings, mode/default helper reuse, affected test updates and deletion of ACP copies. Out: shared store implementation/public API changes (US-001/US-002), lock-holder API (US-003), TUI/directory resolution outside the existing ACP options logic. This story depends only on US-002, not US-003. No new package subpath export and no change to `check:package-boundaries`; the shared storage is exported from the `@nathapp/nax-agent` package entry only. Sessions-dir resolution beyond `defaultSessionsDir(configDir)` stays in the ACP server: `--sessions-dir`, `NAX_AGENT_SESSIONS_DIR` and `agentServer.sessionsDir` are read only by `nax-agent-acp/src/server/options.ts`; how the TUI resolves the directory is decided in feature F3. The transcript store (`createFileTranscriptStore`, `TranscriptStore`) is unchanged and not moved. No mode values are added to `SESSION_META_MODES`; mapping the TUI's `guarded` and `full` modes onto it is feature F3's work. Formats remain unchanged. No release and no version bump.

**Interface** — Verbatim protocol-adapter target:

`toRequestError` (`nax-agent-acp/src/server/errors.ts`) — Target adds, before the
generic branch: `NaxError` code `SESSION_LOCKED` ->
`RequestError.invalidRequest(undefined, error.message)`; `NaxError` code
`SESSION_LIST_CURSOR_INVALID` -> `invalidParams(error.message)`. Neither logs.

Verbatim neutral page declarations consumed from @nathapp/nax-agent:

```typescript
export interface SessionListEntry {
  readonly sessionId: string;
  readonly cwd: string;
  readonly title: string | null;
  readonly updatedAt: string;
}
export interface SessionListPage {
  sessions: SessionListEntry[];
  nextCursor?: string;
}
export function defaultSessionsDir(configDir: string): string; // join(configDir, ".agent-server", "sessions")
export const SESSION_META_MODES = ["none", "read", "ask", "full"] as const;
```

The shared storage list returns Promise<SessionListPage>; the ACP registry remains responsible for ListSessionsResponse. Expected refusal messages preserve their pid or invalid-cursor text on the wire with JSON-RPC codes -32600 and -32602 respectively.
